<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Etchū Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Etchū Province was a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast, corresponding to modern Toyama Prefecture. In the 1570s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Uesugi Kenshin</a> of neighbouring Echigo campaigned there against local lords and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikko-ikki">Ikkō-ikki</a>. After 1600 most of it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeda-clan">Maeda clan</a>, lords of Kaga Domain, the richest domain of the Tokugawa period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/etchu-province.jpg" alt="Etchū Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Etchu.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
